# Line-ending policy for byte-observable repository files.
#
# Deliberately narrow. There is no `* text=auto` here on purpose: several gates
# byte-compare files (G4 reads docs/ENGINE-STATE.md from both a PowerShell and a
# bash script), so a repository-wide renormalization would move far more than it
# fixes. Only files whose *bytes* are observable are pinned.

# Generated state docs are compared against deterministic generated/live output.
# Force LF in every working tree so Windows core.autocrlf cannot manufacture a
# false stale verdict from a clean checkout. See #857.
docs/AUTHORING-STATE.md text eol=lf
docs/ENGINE-STATE.md    text eol=lf

# Geometry sources are text, but their byte count is observable: the Studio model
# picker renders `Math.round(size / 1024) KB` from the on-disk size
# (studio/editor/js/model-picker.js), and that string is captured in the G6 golden
# frame model-picker/item-model.png. With Git's default autocrlf on Windows the
# same commit checks out at a different size than it was stored at, so G6 passed
# in a long-lived checkout and failed in a fresh worktree. See #653.
*.obj -text
*.mtl -text

# Binary assets, pinned explicitly rather than trusting content detection.
# Detection reads only the first 8000 bytes and looks for NUL, so a binary that
# happens to start without one is treated as text and rewritten on checkout.
# That is not hypothetical here: assets/fonts/RobotoMono-Regular.ttf gains 1115
# bytes on checkout today.
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.mid   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.blend binary
*.efkefc binary
*.efk   binary
*.dll   binary
*.love  binary

# The portable item-model toolkit ships its own integrity records:
# TOOLCHAIN_MANIFEST.json stores a byte length and SHA-256 per file, and
# SHA256SUMS.txt repeats the hashes. Both describe the file as it sits on disk,
# so every enumerated file's bytes are observable and must not depend on the
# checkout platform. Unpinned, all sixteen expanded to CRLF on Windows and the
# manifest test was permanently red there while CI stayed green. See #901.
tools/blender/second-rite-item-model-toolkit/**            text eol=lf

# The one exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF, and this file's `if errorlevel 1 ( )`
# block is the construct where LF-only batch files misparse. It is a
# double-click entry point shipped to other people, so it is pinned to CRLF on
# every platform and its manifest entry records that form.
tools/blender/second-rite-item-model-toolkit/BUILD_LIBRARY_WINDOWS.bat  text eol=crlf

# sync_asset_core.py keeps the toolkit's vendor/ copies byte-identical to these
# canonical sources, and a test asserts that equality. Pinning only the vendor
# side would make the two differ by line endings alone on Windows, so the
# originals are pinned to match. See #901.
tools/blender/second_rite_asset_core.py   text eol=lf
tools/asset-language/contract.json        text eol=lf
tools/asset-language/materials.json       text eol=lf
